cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the study design, please cite it as below."
title: "Residual Worlds: residual dynamics learning for data-efficient model-predictive control"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lehner
    given-names: Rene-Marcel
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-27"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RnLe/residual-worlds"
abstract: >-
  A controlled simulation study on a torque-controlled planar two-link arm.
  Under matched scarce target-world transition budgets, it compares unchanged
  nominal physics, bounded fitted physics, a black-box neural dynamics
  ensemble, a physics-residual ensemble, and an exact-dynamics reference,
  all consumed by one frozen CEM-based model-predictive controller, with
  paired closed-loop task success as the primary endpoint.
